          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The Boelen’s python, <i>Simalia</i> <i>boeleni</i>, is a non-venomous snake found only on the island of Papua New Guinea.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 16
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig. 8.1 shows a Boelen’s python.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 16
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "fig8.1",
            "caption": "Fig. 8.1",
            "src": "figures/q8_fig8_1.png",
            "alt": "Python",
            "source": {
              "qp": 16
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) has not assessed the conservation status of <i>S.</i> <i>boeleni</i> because the python is very hard to detect and locate.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 16
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "<i>S.</i> <i>boeleni</i> is listed in one of the appendices of the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES).",
            "source": {
              "qp": 16
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Suggest the advantages of <i>S.</i> <i>boeleni</i> being listed in CITES, even though it does not have an IUCN conservation status.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 16
            }
          }
        ],
